  I followed this entire thread and gave it a try... So today I won with
a Tourist without:
- polypiling (didn't even identify wand of polymorph)
- ring of conflict (I identified three rings in the whole game - stealth,
  see invisible and searching - eventually dumped all of them in hell)
- robbing shops (I don't conunt three or four more or less useless items
  my dog has stolen)
- levitation (yes, it is possible)
- reverse genociding 
- using any abuses (like infinite gold, kicking sinks, bag-of-holding bug,
  paralysing wizard, not to mention save-copy-restore)
- using amulet of life saving (I dumped two of them, kept one against some
  stupid death - but it was not needed)
- bones levels (just happened not to hit any).

  I was level 14 (honestly earned - no gain level and just one wraith -
10->11), had 97 HP, 18/10 STR (15 in the castle, later met some giants),
-20AC (result of wishing, in the castle it was still -8) and +7 Frost Brand
(was +4 most of the time, I found another scroll on my way back). The whole
game took 30000 turns - 10000 too many because I had no mirror! (and the
wizard was two levels below the castle).

  So the point is: you can win without abuses, you can win without
using all the features of the game, and I like it that way (in fact I hate
those games where you have to find everything and solve all the riddles
to win). If anything should be changed in the overall game balance, I
would vote for making low levels a bit easier - I still lose 90% of starting
characters on levels 4-7, and even a very careful play doesn't seem to
help much.

  For the higher levels - they may seem easy, but only if you have a lot
of experience (or spoilers). To survive on low levels you need knowledge
and luck. On higher levels it is just knowledge and experience - and I like
it that way.
